---
title: Char Siu Chicken
servings: 2
prepTime: 10 minutes
cookTime: 20 minutes
Rating: 10/10
source: https://foodielife.eu.org/chinese-style-char-siew-chicken-roast/?utm_source=flipboard&utm_content=topic%2Ffood
tags: Chicken
---

In a #medium bowl{}, mix the @honey{1%tbsp}, @light soy sauce{1%tbsp}, @oyster sauce{1%tbsp}, 
@dark soy sauce{1%tbsp}(or Kecap Manis), @brown sugar{2%tbsp}, @garlic{2%cloves}(minced),
@ginger{1%inch}(fresh grated), @Chinese five spice powder{1%tsp}, and @white pepper{pinch}
together until well combined.
Optionally add @?red food coloring{1%tsp} for the traditional red appearance.

Add the @chicken thighs{10%oz}(boneless, skinless) to the marinade.
Ensure the chicken is fully coated in the marinade by massaging it in.
Let the chicken marinate in the fridge for at least two hours, or overnight for the best results.

Preheat your oven to 400°F.
Line a #baking pan{} with aluminum foil.
This will make cleanup easier as the marinade thickens and becomes sticky during roasting.
Remove the chicken from the marinade, reserving any remaining liquid.
Place the marinated chicken on the prepared pan and roast it in the preheated oven for about ~{15-20%minutes}.

Transfer the reserved marinade to a saucepan and heat it over low heat until it becomes thick and bubbly.
This flavorful sauce will be used as a dipping sauce for the Char Siew Chicken or can be drizzled over rice for added taste.

When the chicken has finished cooking, remove from the oven, and slice into strips.
Serve with the marinade glaze as a dipping sauce, along with cooked @white rice{2%cups}.
